    "body": "I think we should use the port message queue task source, and therefore also amending the transfer-receiving steps to explicitly mention \"close\" events in addition to \"message\" events when it \"Move(s) all the tasks...\".\n\nThis is because we can transfer a MessagePort that still has several messages in its queue and that has been closed by the other side, and it makes sense for all of those messages and then the close event to be fired wherever that MessagePort ends up and that will be very content-observable (versus the messages transferring but the close event firing on the otherwise dead MessagePort in the transferring global).  So I think it's really the only way we can sanely specify it.  Hand-wavingly, I think the case can be made that the ambiguity of the current under-specification might imply this, but it's also incredibly ambiguous, so thank you for undertaking this cleanup!",
    "created_at": "2026-09-22T16:09:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-22T16:09:53Z",
