    "body": "I should also note that while I can only speak from a Gecko perspective, both our current implementation of MessagePorts that used a centralized router model and our/my planned overhaul of MessagePorts that uses direct endpoint connections both favor use of the port message queue task source and re-shipping.  I think it would be a somewhat weird IPC model where it would be easier for an implementation to do the global task that wasn't effectively using the port message queue up until the last second.",
